                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R=[0,\\sqrt2]",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q65-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Require ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0\\le\\sqrt{x-1}\\le2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then rebuild the range through the outer square root.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Both radicands must be non-negative.\n$$\\begin{align*}x-1&\\ge0\\\\x&\\ge1\\\\2-\\sqrt{x-1}&\\ge0\\\\\\sqrt{x-1}&\\le2\\\\x-1&\\le4\\\\x&\\le5\\end{align*}$$\nThus $D=[1,5]$.\n\nOn this domain, the inner square root takes every value in $[0,2]$. Rebuilding the function gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x-1}&\\in[0,2]\\\\2-\\sqrt{x-1}&\\in[0,2]\\\\\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{x-1}}&\\in[0,\\sqrt2].\\end{align*}$$\nBoth endpoints occur: $f(5)=0$ and $f(1)=\\sqrt2$. Therefore $R=[0,\\sqrt2]$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task65-66-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
