        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q66-short-domain",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "D=(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,3]",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q66-short-range",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R=(-\\infty,0)\\cup[2,\\infty)",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q66-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Set ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "t=\\sqrt{3-x}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and consider ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0\\le t<2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "t>2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " separately.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The radicand must be non-negative and the denominator must be non-zero.\n$$\\begin{align*}3-x&\\ge0\\\\x&\\le3\\\\2-\\sqrt{3-x}&\\ne0\\\\\\sqrt{3-x}&\\ne2\\\\3-x&\\ne4\\\\x&\\ne-1\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $D=(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,3]$.\n\nLet $t=\\sqrt{3-x}$. On the domain, $t$ takes every non-negative value except $2$.\n\nFor $0\\le t<2$, the denominator takes every value in $(0,2]$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2-t&\\in(0,2]\\\\\\frac{4}{2-t}&\\in[2,\\infty).\\end{align*}$$\nThe value $2$ occurs when $t=0$, corresponding to $x=3$.\n\nFor $t>2$, the denominator takes every negative value:\n$$\\begin{align*}2-t&\\in(-\\infty,0)\\\\\\frac{4}{2-t}&\\in(-\\infty,0).\\end{align*}$$\nTaking the reciprocal of every negative denominator and multiplying by $4$ gives every negative output; zero is never attained.\n\nHence $R=(-\\infty,0)\\cup[2,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
